  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Top-K Classification Accuracy** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_topk_accuracy(logits: list, targets: list, k: int = 1) -> float:\n    L = np.array(logits, dtype=float)\n    T = np.array(targets, dtype=int)\n    topk = np.argsort(-L, axis=1)[:, :k]\n    return round(float(np.mean([T[i] in topk[i] for i in range(len(T))])), 6)\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
